# Production API base baked into `npm run build` (CRA reads .env.production
# at build time; the value is inlined into the JS bundle).
#
# Default: `/api/v1` (same-origin). Use this when the Worker is routed on the
# same host as Pages (custom domain + Worker route, or Pages Functions).
#
# Override at build time when the Worker is on a separate workers.dev URL:
#
#   cmd /c "set REACT_APP_API_BASE=https://dnd-assistant-api.<your-sub>.workers.dev/api/v1&& npm run build"
#
# (PowerShell's $env: doesn't propagate to react-scripts build child
# processes — use `cmd /c "set ...&& npm run build"` to force it through.
# See CLOUDFLARE-RUNBOOK.md → "What broke" #7 for the long version.)
#
# Whatever you set, also add the Pages origin to
# FRONTEND_CORS_ORIGINS in worker/wrangler.toml and re-deploy the Worker.
REACT_APP_API_BASE=/api/v1